WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:00.990
- Nice to meet you!

00:00:00.990 --> 00:00:01.823
- [Topher] Pleasure to meet you.

00:00:01.823 --> 00:00:02.656
- Yeah, meet Topher,

00:00:02.656 --> 00:00:03.616
he likes cheeseburgers.
- I miss you.

00:00:03.616 --> 00:00:04.680
(guests laughing)

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:05.551
Who doesn't?

00:00:05.551 --> 00:00:06.384
- I know. I miss you too.

00:00:06.384 --> 00:00:07.860
You're always working
though. I'm always working.

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:08.730
- You're always working.

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:09.660
I'm already hooked to the pillow.

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:11.010
- Someone was actually, that's okay.

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:12.300
It's a very cute outfit.

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:13.133
- Thanks.

00:00:13.133 --> 00:00:15.051
It's giving a little
bit of yee-haw energy.

00:00:15.051 --> 00:00:15.884
Had to do it.
- Love it.

00:00:15.884 --> 00:00:17.460
It's like yee-haw and rock and roll.

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:18.930
Plus some business.
- A little Harry Styles

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:20.040
moment, too.

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:21.240
- And that's always a good moment.

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:22.073
I like his style.
- It is.

00:00:22.073 --> 00:00:24.330
He is the moment.
- No pun intended.

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:25.920
People were asking me backstage,

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:27.180
they were like, "You've
known her for a while."

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:29.280
I was like, yes, I've
known her for a while.

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:30.921
- And now, we have a song together.

00:00:30.921 --> 00:00:32.220
- (gasps) We do.

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:33.780
Me, you, and Carly Pearce.

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:34.740
- We do. It just came out.

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:37.050
- I can't actually tell
that full story on TV,

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:41.550
but it's quite funny, that
recording day for me. (laughs)

00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:45.000
- I asked Kelly to be a part
of my song in the morning,

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:47.220
and she went to the studio
that night and did vocals.

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:48.261
- Wow.

00:00:48.261 --> 00:00:53.261
- So, you know what, I'm gonna
give you a little bit of it.

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:56.760
So, it's my last day of work.

00:00:56.760 --> 00:00:59.647
I have told Trisha, my assistant
and my group, I'm like,

00:00:59.647 --> 00:01:00.600
"I can't do anything."

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:01.530
I will not.
- The day I texted you?

00:01:01.530 --> 00:01:02.610
- The day you texted me.

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:03.690
I had literally been like, look,

00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:04.828
this has to be my last day, then I'm off.

00:01:04.828 --> 00:01:06.780
I was like, I promised myself this summer.

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:08.850
And not only you text
me, but Shane McAnally,

00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:10.200
our friend who's also a singer-songwriter.

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:12.390
And, anyway he, you both texted me,

00:01:12.390 --> 00:01:13.223
and they were like, "Oh we got this song."

00:01:13.223 --> 00:01:14.340
And I was like, oh, I love Kelsea.

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:16.020
I was like, okay, lemme just listen to it.

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:18.480
And I was like, oh, I have to do this.

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:22.683
Well, I had already been celebrating-

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:24.600
- I do know this story.

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:26.490
- I had already been celebrating that it

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:28.293
was my last day of work.

00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:32.700
Mkay, so I get to the studio,

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:35.040
here at this studio with Jason,

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:36.940
and I get in there and I'm like, look,

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:39.830
I didn't know I was
gonna be singing today.

00:01:39.830 --> 00:01:42.810
I was like, I don't know, so I had to sing

00:01:42.810 --> 00:01:47.810
a song called 'You're
Drunk Go Home' inebriated,

00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:51.750
trying to sing for soprano
parts like I'm fine.

00:01:51.750 --> 00:01:54.300
Like, there is an actual full track,

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:56.610
we have to send it to
you, of me just crying

00:01:56.610 --> 00:01:58.440
and laughing so hard I
almost peed my pants.

00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:00.000
- Please do.
- 'Cause I was like,

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:01.680
this has never happened to me in 20 years.

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:05.070
I've never ever been inebriated
while singing something,

00:02:05.070 --> 00:02:08.702
and I am while singing
'You're Drunk Go Home'.

00:02:08.702 --> 00:02:11.047
- There is this mo-

00:02:11.047 --> 00:02:11.880
(audience cheering)

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:13.045
- It's a great song.

00:02:13.045 --> 00:02:14.880
It's a great song.

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:15.713
- There's one ad lib

00:02:15.713 --> 00:02:16.920
on the track.
- I didn't know,

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:19.470
I had already started and then you texted.

00:02:19.470 --> 00:02:23.190
- There's one part on
the song where it's like

00:02:23.190 --> 00:02:25.230
an ad lib track and now
you're gonna hear it

00:02:25.230 --> 00:02:26.397
and now you're gonna know.

00:02:26.397 --> 00:02:28.097
And you just hear Kelly go, "Bye."

00:02:29.850 --> 00:02:32.160
And it's in there and it's cranked.

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:33.330
So thank you for that.

00:02:33.330 --> 00:02:34.696
- You're welcome.

00:02:34.696 --> 00:02:35.529
- Thank you for that.

00:02:35.529 --> 00:02:37.112
- I was like, I felt so bad.

00:02:37.112 --> 00:02:38.901
Has that ever happened to you?

00:02:38.901 --> 00:02:39.933
- On set, have you ever?
- I didn't know!

00:02:39.933 --> 00:02:41.580
No, because I would

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:42.464
never do it.
- Oh, I'm drunk

00:02:42.464 --> 00:02:43.297
every time you see me.
- Every time.

00:02:43.297 --> 00:02:44.250
- He's drunk right now.

00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:46.770
No, I just, nobody had told me.

00:02:46.770 --> 00:02:48.330
So I'd already celebrated
and then I got it

00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:49.800
and it was already too late.

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:51.990
- I just, I gotta hear this song.

00:02:51.990 --> 00:02:53.370
- It's a great song.

00:02:53.370 --> 00:02:54.203
It's a great song.

00:02:54.203 --> 00:02:55.860
- Yeah, it's meant to
feel kind of like you're

00:02:55.860 --> 00:02:57.927
at a bar anyway.
- I was at an

00:02:57.927 --> 00:02:59.094
actual bar.
- Bar.

00:02:59.094 --> 00:03:02.370
- Yeah, and it turned out so funny.

00:03:02.370 --> 00:03:03.900
Okay, I wanna talk about
your new album now.

00:03:03.900 --> 00:03:05.580
I love the title, 'Subject to Change'.

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:06.540
- Yeah, thanks.
- This is a,

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:08.520
I think titles are everything,

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:09.780
'cause you kind of have to encompass

00:03:09.780 --> 00:03:11.340
what all is happening on it.

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:12.870
And I love it.

00:03:12.870 --> 00:03:13.703
- Thank you.
- So like,

00:03:13.703 --> 00:03:14.820
why 'Subject to Change?'

00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:16.020
Why does that count?

00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:18.300
- Every record I've gotten
to make has kind of been

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:19.710
a snapshot of like the two years

00:03:19.710 --> 00:03:21.496
of my twenties that I wrote it during.

00:03:21.496 --> 00:03:24.390
And when I was listening to
the demos I was like, man,

00:03:24.390 --> 00:03:28.650
I'm writing a lot about kind
of like this stark contrast

00:03:28.650 --> 00:03:32.010
and juxtaposition that I've
been feeling as I've grown up

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:34.353
and entered into my late twenties and so,

00:03:35.310 --> 00:03:40.020
I just, I loved the idea of
taking the polarizing feeling

00:03:40.020 --> 00:03:41.850
and the fear away from the word, 'change',

00:03:41.850 --> 00:03:43.530
and going like, if I just embrace it,

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:45.480
'cause it's gonna happen inevitably, like,

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:46.680
can I find joy in it?

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:47.998
And it's kind of that journey.

00:03:47.998 --> 00:03:50.610
- I actually do find joy in change.

00:03:50.610 --> 00:03:52.380
And I don't know if it's
from childhood trauma

00:03:52.380 --> 00:03:53.213
where a lot of change happened.

00:03:53.213 --> 00:03:54.420
- Same.

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:56.220
- You know, a lot of
change happened regardless

00:03:56.220 --> 00:03:57.417
of me wanting it, you know?

00:03:57.417 --> 00:04:00.660
Or the desire, but I think
it actually did enable me

00:04:00.660 --> 00:04:03.120
to like embrace it rather
than be so fearful.

00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:05.610
'Cause people can be
very fearful of change.

00:04:05.610 --> 00:04:06.870
I love it. What about you?

00:04:06.870 --> 00:04:07.703
Are you good with change

00:04:07.703 --> 00:04:08.716
or no?
- No, I fear change.

00:04:08.716 --> 00:04:09.595
(audience laughing)

00:04:09.595 --> 00:04:10.680
- I love you so much.

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:11.580
- But I mean, we all fear change.

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:12.750
We're trying to embrace it, right?

00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:15.150
- Yeah, it's a journey.
- I don't. I don't fear it.

00:04:15.150 --> 00:04:17.675
I think because of whenever
I was younger just so much,

00:04:17.675 --> 00:04:20.790
that I just had to kind
of learn that it could,

00:04:20.790 --> 00:04:22.320
'cause you never, I think people fear it

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:23.820
because you don't know what's
on the other side, right?

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:24.653
You don't know

00:04:24.653 --> 00:04:25.486
what's gonna happen.
- I always think this too

00:04:25.486 --> 00:04:28.740
shall pass and that means,
you know, good things will,

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:31.650
that will pass but also bad
things will pass too, right?

00:04:31.650 --> 00:04:33.570
- Or come. (laughs)

00:04:33.570 --> 00:04:35.010
You're like, eh.

00:04:35.010 --> 00:04:37.620
But you recently went back
to your high school reunion.

00:04:37.620 --> 00:04:39.090
I never got to do that.
- I did.

00:04:39.090 --> 00:04:40.170
- I didn't even know mine happened.

00:04:40.170 --> 00:04:43.050
So, like, so yeah, what was that like?

00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:44.889
Were they freaking out?

00:04:44.889 --> 00:04:47.700
- It was half and half, I gotta be honest.

00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:48.870
So this was the high school

00:04:48.870 --> 00:04:51.450
that I left after my sophomore
year to move to Nashville

00:04:51.450 --> 00:04:52.283
to do this.

00:04:52.283 --> 00:04:53.910
So I didn't graduate here.

00:04:53.910 --> 00:04:56.730
So I was kind of like an honorary bobcat.

00:04:56.730 --> 00:05:01.730
But my best friend graduated
from there and I went with her

00:05:02.430 --> 00:05:05.640
and it was so interesting
'cause we walked in the room

00:05:05.640 --> 00:05:09.087
and people were having dinner
and it was the same people.

00:05:09.087 --> 00:05:10.533
- Cliques?
- At the tables!

00:05:11.970 --> 00:05:14.910
Yeah, that was after we drank.

00:05:14.910 --> 00:05:17.310
- Yeah, see this is, by the
way, this is what it looked like

00:05:17.310 --> 00:05:20.310
in the studio when I was
recording 'You're Drunk Go Home'.

00:05:20.310 --> 00:05:21.143
- This is why we're friends.

00:05:21.143 --> 00:05:22.756
- Yeah, yeah, we're similar.

00:05:22.756 --> 00:05:25.320
- It was really beautiful
because it was actually

00:05:25.320 --> 00:05:28.140
the 11 year reunion and
it was just really cool

00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:30.600
to see everyone and everyone's
in a different phase of life

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:32.790
but, you know, we're all
just growing up and it's like

00:05:32.790 --> 00:05:35.520
a really cool, it was really,
I don't know, heartfelt.

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:36.820
- Oh I love that.

00:05:36.820 --> 00:05:38.730
I didn't even know mine existed.

00:05:38.730 --> 00:05:39.960
Whenever they were.

00:05:39.960 --> 00:05:42.540
I'm like old now so
there's probably been many.

00:05:42.540 --> 00:05:44.310
But wait, were you, what
were you like in high school?

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:46.320
We know you weren't as
popular as Frank but-

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:47.733
- Yeah, Frank.

00:05:49.020 --> 00:05:49.853
- [Kelly] How was it?

00:05:49.853 --> 00:05:51.661
- I went to a boarding
school so I loved it.

00:05:51.661 --> 00:05:53.430
But I wanted to go, it
wasn't one of those,

00:05:53.430 --> 00:05:54.750
a lot of people think when I tell them

00:05:54.750 --> 00:05:56.520
that I was sent there by my parents.

00:05:56.520 --> 00:05:58.650
But I actually enjoyed
it and wanted to go.

00:05:58.650 --> 00:06:00.810
And it was kind of like mini college.

00:06:00.810 --> 00:06:01.740
But who's the guy?

00:06:01.740 --> 00:06:04.290
Who was the guy who
you saw at your reunion

00:06:04.290 --> 00:06:06.660
who you said, now I'm this person?

00:06:06.660 --> 00:06:07.530
- Was there a guy?

00:06:07.530 --> 00:06:08.363
- There wasn't a guy.

00:06:08.363 --> 00:06:09.972
- Oh, come on.
- Was there a girl?

00:06:09.972 --> 00:06:10.805
Wait, was that? I was like, wait, what?

00:06:10.805 --> 00:06:14.220
- It's 'cause I always dated older guys.

00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:15.180
- Yeah so.

00:06:15.180 --> 00:06:17.929
- That's also a little
bit of childhood trauma.

00:06:17.929 --> 00:06:20.027
(Kelsea laughs)

00:06:20.027 --> 00:06:20.860
Me too.

00:06:20.860 --> 00:06:22.460
- Okay.

00:06:22.460 --> 00:06:24.270
Oh well, no segue there.

00:06:24.270 --> 00:06:26.340
We need to take a break but stick around

00:06:26.340 --> 00:06:28.230
because Kelsea and her band are performing

00:06:28.230 --> 00:06:29.063
for us later in the show.

00:06:29.063 --> 00:06:30.960
It's such a great song,
you'll wanna see it.

00:06:30.960 --> 00:06:33.690
Once again, her new album is
called 'Subject to Change'.

00:06:33.690 --> 00:06:36.033
It is, it's out now.

